[?2004l[?2004h> s=open(p).read().replace('bin/clinicops overlaps\n', 'bin/clinicops overlaps\nbin/clinicops remind [--now RFC3339]\n')
[?2004l[?2004h> s=s.replace('`64` usage.', '`64` usage. `remind` exits `3` if any SMS send fails (and continues with the other\nappointments).')
[?2004l[?2004h> s += '''
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Appointment reminders
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> Run `clinicops remind` from cron every 15 minutes. `--now RFC3339` pins the clock
[?2004l[?2004h> for a replay or test. It sends SMS reminders for booked appointments starting in
[?2004l[?2004h> `(now, now + 24 hours]` when the patient has SMS consent and a phone number, and
[?2004l[?2004h> only between 08:00 (inclusive) and 21:00 (exclusive) in each appointment clinic's
[?2004l[?2004h> time zone. Quiet-hour reminders wait until an eligible daytime run; appointments
[?2004l[?2004h> that have already started are never reminded.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> Relaywave receives the clinic's `sms_template` with nested `patient`, `appointment`,
[?2004l[?2004h> `clinician` and `clinic` records in `vars`, plus `appointment.starts_local` (for
[?2004l[?2004h> example, `Tue 17 Nov, 09:30`). No local template export is required.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> Successful deliveries are saved in `$CLINIC_DATA/reminders_sent.json`, keyed by
[?2004l[?2004h> appointment ID and start instant, so moving an appointment to a new start makes it
[?2004l[?2004h> eligible again. Keep this file between runs. Failed sends are not recorded and
[?2004l[?2004h> will be retried on the next eligible run. A `reminders_sent.lock` file serializes
[?2004l[?2004h> overlapping runs. Output lists `reminded <id>` for each success in start-time
[?2004l[?2004h> order, followed by `sent <n>`.
[?2004l[?2004h> '''
[?2004l[?2004h> open(p,'w').write(s)
[?2004l[?2004h> PY
